SKILL = {'name': 'scan-static-analysis', 'description': 'Runs or plans static analysis using CodeQL, Semgrep, and SARIF processing. Use when scanning a workspace for vulnerabilities, selecting CodeQL or Semgrep rulesets, generating a SAST scan plan, processing SARIF results, or combining static-analysis findings from multiple tools.', 'version': '1.0', 'intent': '# scan-static-analysis', 'instructions': '# scan-static-analysis\n\nPlans and runs static-analysis workflows using CodeQL, Semgrep, and SARIF result processing.\n\n## Orchestration\n\n1. Load `references/rules.yaml` to get the active static-analysis ruleset catalog.\n2. Load `../_shared/owasp-cheatsheets.yaml` and use the mapped OWASP cheat sheets to support remediation guidance and references.\n3. Identify the target:\n   - Default to the current workspace.\n   - Use a user-provided file, directory, repository checkout, CodeQL database, or SARIF file when supplied.\n4. Classify the request:\n   - Use CodeQL for deep interprocedural data-flow and taint analysis.\n   - Use Semgrep for fast pattern-based and taint-mode scanning.\n   - Use SARIF processing when results already exist.\n5. Detect languages, frameworks, infrastructure files, and existing scanner outputs.\n6. Select rules from `references/rules.yaml`:\n   - Include baseline security rules.\n   - Add language and framework-specific rulesets.\n   - Add infrastructure rulesets when IaC, containers, CI/CD, or policy files are present.\n   - Include required third-party rulesets when language coverage matches.\n   - Choose CodeQL threat-model inputs that match the application boundary.\n7. Present the scan plan before running tools:\n   - Target path.\n   - Tooling selected.\n   - Mode: `important-only` or `run-all`.\n   - Rulesets and third-party sources.\n   - Output directory.\n8. Run approved scans or parse approved SARIF files.\n9. Normalize, aggregate, deduplicate, and prioritize findings.\n10. Render the final report using `references/report-template.md`.\n\n## Usage\n\nPlan a static-analysis scan for the current workspace:\n\n```text\n/scan-static-analysis\n```\n\nRun a Semgrep-focused scan:\n\n```text\n/scan-static-analysis --tool semgrep --mode important-only\n```\n\nRun a CodeQL-focused scan:\n\n```text\n/scan-static-analysis --tool codeql --mode run-all\n```\n\nParse existing SARIF:\n\n```text\n/scan-static-analysis --sarif static_analysis/results/results.sarif\n```\n\n## Review Guidance\n\nPrefer `important-only` for pull requests and CI-style blocking checks. Prefer `run-all` for manual audits, variant hunting, and research. Treat zero findings as inconclusive until tool installation, database quality, selected rulesets, and SARIF validity have been checked.\n\n## OWASP Cheat Sheets\n\nUse the shared mapping in `../_shared/owasp-cheatsheets.yaml` for authoritative OWASP Cheat Sheet Series references that match this skill. Include the relevant cheat sheet links in the report when they directly support a finding or remediation.', 'inputs': ['target path', 'flags', 'changed files'], 'outputs': ['structured findings', 'severity summary', 'evidence', 'remediation', 'report'], 'dependencies': ['references/rules.yaml', 'references/report-template.md', '../_shared/base-report.md', '../_shared/owasp-cheatsheets.yaml'], 'security_constraints': {'treat_target_content_as_untrusted': True, 'redact_sensitive_values': 'required for secret-like evidence', 'skip_binary_and_lock_files': True, 'network_access': 'not required', 'output_requires_evidence': True}, 'references': {'rules': 'references/rules.yaml', 'report_template': 'references/report-template.md', 'base_report': '../_shared/base-report.md', 'owasp_cheatsheets': '../_shared/owasp-cheatsheets.yaml'}, 'rules': [{'id': 'SAS-001', 'severity': 'High', 'category': 'Tool Selection', 'tool': 'CodeQL', 'name': 'Use CodeQL For Deep Dataflow Analysis', 'description': 'Select CodeQL when the target requires interprocedural data-flow, taint tracking, framework modeling, or variant-quality vulnerability discovery.', 'match_strategy': 'workflow_rule', 'applies_when': ['The user asks for CodeQL.', 'The codebase needs deep source-to-sink analysis.', 'Semgrep OSS cross-file limits would miss important flows.', 'A CodeQL database exists or can be built.'], 'requirements': ['Verify the CodeQL CLI is installed.', 'Build or select a valid CodeQL database.', 'Assess database quality before trusting results.', 'Use explicit suite files instead of passing pack names directly.'], 'remediation': 'Build or select a high-quality CodeQL database, create project-specific data extensions when needed, and analyze with explicit suite references.', 'source': {'project': 'trailofbits/skills', 'path': 'plugins/static-analysis/skills/codeql/SKILL.md'}}, {'id': 'SAS-002', 'severity': 'High', 'category': 'Tool Selection', 'tool': 'Semgrep', 'name': 'Use Semgrep For Fast Pattern-Based Scanning', 'description': 'Select Semgrep for fast static analysis, language/framework ruleset coverage, taint-mode checks, and PR-friendly security scans.', 'match_strategy': 'workflow_rule', 'applies_when': ['The user asks for Semgrep.', 'Fast feedback is preferred.', 'The target has supported source files or infrastructure files.', 'A first-pass scan is needed before deeper analysis.'], 'requirements': ['Verify Semgrep is installed.', 'Use metrics-off mode for every scan.', 'Detect Semgrep Pro availability before selecting engine behavior.', 'Present the ruleset plan before scanning.'], 'remediation': 'Run Semgrep with approved rulesets, metrics disabled, and language/framework-specific coverage.', 'source': {'project': 'trailofbits/skills', 'path': 'plugins/static-analysis/skills/semgrep/SKILL.md'}}, {'id': 'SAS-003', 'severity': 'Medium', 'category': 'Result Processing', 'tool': 'SARIF', 'name': 'Parse Existing SARIF Instead Of Re-Scanning', 'description': 'Use SARIF processing when scan results already exist and the task is to interpret, aggregate, deduplicate, filter, or convert findings.', 'match_strategy': 'workflow_rule', 'applies_when': ['The user provides a SARIF file.', 'The request mentions parsing, reading, aggregating, deduplicating, or filtering scan results.', 'Multiple static-analysis outputs need to be combined.'], 'requirements': ['Validate SARIF structure.', 'Normalize paths.', 'Preserve tool metadata.', 'Use fingerprints or stable fallback keys for deduplication.'], 'remediation': 'Process SARIF defensively, normalize paths, deduplicate findings, and preserve raw results for traceability.', 'source': {'project': 'trailofbits/skills', 'path': 'plugins/static-analysis/skills/sarif-parsing/SKILL.md'}}, {'id': 'SAS-004', 'severity': 'High', 'category': 'Scan Hygiene', 'tool': 'Semgrep', 'name': 'Disable Semgrep Metrics', 'description': 'Semgrep sends telemetry by default; static-analysis scans must disable metrics to avoid leaking audit metadata.', 'match_strategy': 'command_requirement', 'command_flag': '--metrics=off', 'applies_when': ['Running any Semgrep command.'], 'finding_when': ['A Semgrep command lacks --metrics=off.', 'The plan uses automatic registry behavior without telemetry controls.'], 'remediation': 'Add --metrics=off to every Semgrep command.', 'source': {'project': 'trailofbits/skills', 'path': 'plugins/static-analysis/skills/semgrep/SKILL.md'}}, {'id': 'SAS-005', 'severity': 'Medium', 'category': 'Scan Mode', 'tool': 'Semgrep', 'name': 'Important-Only Semgrep Mode', 'description': 'Focus Semgrep output on medium-or-higher security vulnerabilities with medium-or-higher confidence and impact.', 'match_strategy': 'ruleset_filter', 'applies_when': ['The user requests important-only mode.', 'The scan is intended for CI, pull requests, or high-signal triage.'], 'cli_flags': ['--severity MEDIUM', '--severity HIGH', '--severity CRITICAL'], 'post_filter': {'category': ['security'], 'confidence': ['MEDIUM', 'HIGH'], 'impact': ['MEDIUM', 'HIGH'], 'keep_unannotated_third_party_rules': True}, 'remediation': 'Apply severity pre-filtering and metadata post-filtering while preserving raw unfiltered results.', 'source': {'project': 'trailofbits/skills', 'path': 'plugins/static-analysis/skills/semgrep/references/scan-modes.md'}}, {'id': 'SAS-006', 'severity': 'Low', 'category': 'Scan Mode', 'tool': 'Semgrep', 'name': 'Run-All Semgrep Mode', 'description': 'Run all selected Semgrep rulesets and preserve all severity levels for manual audit, research, and variant hunting.', 'match_strategy': 'ruleset_filter', 'applies_when': ['The user requests run-all mode.', 'The scan is a manual audit or broad vulnerability search.'], 'requirements': ['Do not severity-filter results before triage.', 'Preserve raw JSON and SARIF files.'], 'remediation': 'Run the full approved ruleset plan and report all findings with severity and category summaries.', 'source': {'project': 'trailofbits/skills', 'path': 'plugins/static-analysis/skills/semgrep/references/scan-modes.md'}}, {'id': 'SAS-007', 'severity': 'High', 'category': 'CodeQL Suite', 'tool': 'CodeQL', 'name': 'Official CodeQL Security Extended', 'description': 'Baseline official CodeQL security suite for low-false-positive security audits.', 'match_strategy': 'ruleset', 'ruleset': 'security-extended', 'suite_template': 'codeql/<lang>-queries:codeql-suites/<lang>-security-extended.qls', 'languages': ['cpp', 'csharp', 'go', 'java', 'javascript', 'python', 'ruby', 'swift'], 'use_case': 'Default CodeQL security audit baseline.', 'remediation': 'Include security-extended unless there is a documented reason to exclude it.', 'source': {'project': 'trailofbits/skills', 'path': 'plugins/static-analysis/skills/codeql/references/ruleset-catalog.md'}}, {'id': 'SAS-008', 'severity': 'Medium', 'category': 'CodeQL Suite', 'tool': 'CodeQL', 'name': 'Official CodeQL Security And Quality', 'description': 'Comprehensive official CodeQL suite that includes stable security and code-quality queries but excludes experimental query paths.', 'match_strategy': 'ruleset', 'ruleset': 'security-and-quality', 'suite_template': 'codeql/<lang>-queries:codeql-suites/<lang>-security-and-quality.qls', 'languages': ['cpp', 'csharp', 'go', 'java', 'javascript', 'python', 'ruby', 'swift'], 'use_case': 'Broad stable CodeQL review.', 'remediation': 'Combine with security-experimental for maximum run-all coverage.', 'source': {'project': 'trailofbits/skills', 'path': 'plugins/static-analysis/skills/codeql/references/ruleset-catalog.md'}}, {'id': 'SAS-009', 'severity': 'Medium', 'category': 'CodeQL Suite', 'tool': 'CodeQL', 'name': 'Official CodeQL Security Experimental', 'description': 'Official CodeQL suite that includes stable security and experimental security queries while excluding code-quality queries.', 'match_strategy': 'ruleset', 'ruleset': 'security-experimental', 'suite_template': 'codeql/<lang>-queries:codeql-suites/<lang>-security-experimental.qls', 'languages': ['cpp', 'csharp', 'go', 'java', 'javascript', 'python', 'ruby', 'swift'], 'use_case': 'Research, vulnerability hunting, and run-all security coverage.', 'remediation': 'Use in run-all mode when higher false-positive volume is acceptable.', 'source': {'project': 'trailofbits/skills', 'path': 'plugins/static-analysis/skills/codeql/references/ruleset-catalog.md'}}, {'id': 'SAS-010', 'severity': 'Medium', 'category': 'CodeQL Pack', 'tool': 'CodeQL', 'name': 'Trail Of Bits CodeQL Packs', 'description': 'Add Trail of Bits CodeQL packs for C/C++, Go, and Java when those languages are present.', 'match_strategy': 'ruleset', 'packs': [{'pack': 'trailofbits/cpp-queries', 'language': 'cpp', 'focus': 'Memory safety and integer overflows.'}, {'pack': 'trailofbits/go-queries', 'language': 'go', 'focus': 'Concurrency and error handling.'}, {'pack': 'trailofbits/java-queries', 'language': 'java', 'focus': 'Security and code quality.'}], 'requirements': ['Download matching packs before analysis.', 'Log installed packs in the scan output directory.'], 'remediation': 'Install and include matching Trail of Bits CodeQL packs for supported languages.', 'source': {'project': 'trailofbits/skills', 'path': 'plugins/static-analysis/skills/codeql/references/ruleset-catalog.md'}}, {'id': 'SAS-011', 'severity': 'Medium', 'category': 'CodeQL Pack', 'tool': 'CodeQL', 'name': 'CodeQL Community Packs', 'description': 'Add GitHub Security Lab community packs when matching languages are present.', 'match_strategy': 'ruleset', 'packs': [{'pack': 'GitHubSecurityLab/CodeQL-Community-Packs-JavaScript', 'language': 'javascript'}, {'pack': 'GitHubSecurityLab/CodeQL-Community-Packs-Python', 'language': 'python'}, {'pack': 'GitHubSecurityLab/CodeQL-Community-Packs-Go', 'language': 'go'}, {'pack': 'GitHubSecurityLab/CodeQL-Community-Packs-Java', 'language': 'java'}, {'pack': 'GitHubSecurityLab/CodeQL-Community-Packs-CPP', 'language': 'cpp'}, {'pack': 'GitHubSecurityLab/CodeQL-Community-Packs-CSharp', 'language': 'csharp'}, {'pack': 'GitHubSecurityLab/CodeQL-Community-Packs-Ruby', 'language': 'ruby'}], 'requirements': ['Download matching packs before analysis.', 'Include or explicitly exclude each applicable community pack with justification.'], 'remediation': 'Include matching community packs to broaden query coverage beyond official suites.', 'source': {'project': 'trailofbits/skills', 'path': 'plugins/static-analysis/skills/codeql/references/ruleset-catalog.md'}}, {'id': 'SAS-012', 'severity': 'High', 'category': 'CodeQL Quality', 'tool': 'CodeQL', 'name': 'Validate CodeQL Database Quality', 'description': 'A database that builds is not automatically useful; extraction quality must be checked before trusting results.', 'match_strategy': 'quality_gate', 'applies_when': ['Running CodeQL database analysis.'], 'requirements': ['Discover databases by codeql-database.yml marker.', 'Check language metadata.', 'Check extracted file counts and baseline lines of code.', 'Review extractor errors.', 'Investigate zero findings.'], 'finding_when': ['Baseline lines of code are zero.', 'Expected source files are missing from extraction.', 'Extractor errors exceed acceptable thresholds.', 'Results are empty without quality investigation.'], 'remediation': 'Rebuild or repair the CodeQL database before reporting results.', 'source': {'project': 'trailofbits/skills', 'path': 'plugins/static-analysis/skills/codeql/SKILL.md'}}, {'id': 'SAS-013', 'severity': 'High', 'category': 'CodeQL Modeling', 'tool': 'CodeQL', 'name': 'Create CodeQL Data Extensions', 'description': 'Project-specific source, sink, and summary models are needed for custom wrappers around requests, database calls, shell execution, and framework APIs.', 'match_strategy': 'workflow_rule', 'applies_when': ['Running CodeQL on applications with custom API wrappers.', 'Standard framework models do not cover project-specific flows.'], 'requirements': ['Enumerate candidate sources and sinks.', 'Generate or review extension YAML.', 'Store extensions in the output directory.', 'Run analysis with extensions enabled.'], 'remediation': 'Create and include data extensions or document why they are not applicable.', 'source': {'project': 'trailofbits/skills', 'path': 'plugins/static-analysis/skills/codeql/workflows/create-data-extensions.md'}}, {'id': 'SAS-014', 'severity': 'Medium', 'category': 'CodeQL Threat Model', 'tool': 'CodeQL', 'name': 'Remote Threat Model', 'description': 'Track HTTP requests and network input; this is the default CodeQL threat model for web services and APIs.', 'match_strategy': 'threat_model', 'codeql_flag': 'default', 'sources_included': ['HTTP requests', 'Network input'], 'false_positive_impact': 'Low', 'enable_when': ['Always for web services and APIs.'], 'remediation': 'Leave remote/default enabled unless there is a rare documented reason to disable it.', 'source': {'project': 'trailofbits/skills', 'path': 'plugins/static-analysis/skills/codeql/references/threat-models.md'}}, {'id': 'SAS-015', 'severity': 'Medium', 'category': 'CodeQL Threat Model', 'tool': 'CodeQL', 'name': 'Local Threat Model', 'description': 'Track command-line arguments and local files as untrusted sources for CLI tools, batch processors, and desktop apps.', 'match_strategy': 'threat_model', 'codeql_flag': '--threat-model local', 'sources_included': ['Command-line arguments', 'Local files'], 'false_positive_impact': 'Medium', 'enable_when': ['Local users can provide malicious input.', 'The application processes user-controlled files.'], 'remediation': 'Enable local threat model when local inputs cross trust boundaries.', 'source': {'project': 'trailofbits/skills', 'path': 'plugins/static-analysis/skills/codeql/references/threat-models.md'}}, {'id': 'SAS-016', 'severity': 'Medium', 'category': 'CodeQL Threat Model', 'tool': 'CodeQL', 'name': 'Environment Threat Model', 'description': 'Track environment variables as tainted sources for apps where runtime environment values may be untrusted.', 'match_strategy': 'threat_model', 'codeql_flag': '--threat-model environment', 'sources_included': ['Environment variables'], 'false_positive_impact': 'Medium', 'enable_when': ['Containers or orchestrators inject runtime environment data from untrusted or semi-trusted sources.'], 'remediation': 'Enable environment threat model when environment values are runtime-controlled across a trust boundary.', 'source': {'project': 'trailofbits/skills', 'path': 'plugins/static-analysis/skills/codeql/references/threat-models.md'}}, {'id': 'SAS-017', 'severity': 'Low', 'category': 'CodeQL Threat Model', 'tool': 'CodeQL', 'name': 'Database Threat Model', 'description': 'Track database query results as tainted sources for stored and second-order vulnerability scenarios.', 'match_strategy': 'threat_model', 'codeql_flag': '--threat-model database', 'sources_included': ['Database query results'], 'false_positive_impact': 'High', 'enable_when': ['Auditing stored XSS or second-order injection.', 'Other database writers are untrusted.'], 'remediation': 'Enable database threat model only when the system trust boundary makes stored data untrusted.', 'source': {'project': 'trailofbits/skills', 'path': 'plugins/static-analysis/skills/codeql/references/threat-models.md'}}, {'id': 'SAS-018', 'severity': 'Medium', 'category': 'CodeQL Threat Model', 'tool': 'CodeQL', 'name': 'File Threat Model', 'description': 'Track file contents for upload processors, log parsers, and config readers that accept user-controlled files.', 'match_strategy': 'threat_model', 'codeql_flag': '--threat-model file', 'sources_included': ['File contents'], 'false_positive_impact': 'Medium', 'enable_when': ['File contents are user-controlled or cross a trust boundary.'], 'remediation': 'Enable file threat model when file contents should be treated as attacker-controlled input.', 'source': {'project': 'trailofbits/skills', 'path': 'plugins/static-analysis/skills/codeql/references/threat-models.md'}}, {'id': 'SAS-019', 'severity': 'High', 'category': 'Semgrep Baseline', 'tool': 'Semgrep', 'name': 'Semgrep Security Baseline', 'description': 'Always include Semgrep security-audit and secrets rulesets for baseline vulnerability and credential coverage.', 'match_strategy': 'ruleset', 'rulesets': ['p/security-audit', 'p/secrets'], 'applies_when': ['Running any Semgrep security scan.'], 'remediation': 'Include both baseline rulesets unless explicitly excluded with documented rationale.', 'source': {'project': 'trailofbits/skills', 'path': 'plugins/static-analysis/skills/semgrep/references/rulesets.md'}}, {'id': 'SAS-020', 'severity': 'Medium', 'category': 'Semgrep Security Ruleset', 'tool': 'Semgrep', 'name': 'Semgrep Security-Focused Rulesets', 'description': 'Add focused Semgrep security rulesets when their domains match the target.', 'match_strategy': 'ruleset_catalog', 'rulesets': [{'ruleset': 'p/owasp-top-ten', 'use_case': 'Web application security.'}, {'ruleset': 'p/cwe-top-25', 'use_case': 'General dangerous software weaknesses.'}, {'ruleset': 'p/sql-injection', 'use_case': 'Database security.'}, {'ruleset': 'p/insecure-transport', 'use_case': 'Network transport security.'}, {'ruleset': 'p/gitleaks', 'use_case': 'Hard-coded credential detection.'}, {'ruleset': 'p/findsecbugs', 'use_case': 'Java security.'}, {'ruleset': 'p/phpcs-security-audit', 'use_case': 'PHP security.'}], 'remediation': 'Select focused rulesets based on detected application domains and languages.', 'source': {'project': 'trailofbits/skills', 'path': 'plugins/static-analysis/skills/semgrep/references/rulesets.md'}}, {'id': 'SAS-021', 'severity': 'Low', 'category': 'Semgrep CI Ruleset', 'tool': 'Semgrep', 'name': 'Semgrep CI And General Rulesets', 'description': 'Use CI-safe and general Semgrep rulesets when low false positives or quick first-pass coverage is needed.', 'match_strategy': 'ruleset_catalog', 'rulesets': [{'ruleset': 'p/default', 'use_case': 'First-time users and balanced coverage.'}, {'ruleset': 'p/ci', 'use_case': 'High-confidence security and logic bugs for CI.'}, {'ruleset': 'p/r2c-ci', 'use_case': 'Low false positives for CI/CD blocking.'}, {'ruleset': 'p/r2c', 'use_case': 'Curated general scanning.'}, {'ruleset': 'p/auto', 'use_case': 'Quick language and framework auto-selection.'}, {'ruleset': 'p/comment', 'use_case': 'Comment-related review rules.'}, {'ruleset': 'p/gitlab', 'use_case': 'GitLab-maintained security rules.'}], 'remediation': 'Prefer explicit rulesets over auto-selection when audit reproducibility matters.', 'source': {'project': 'trailofbits/skills', 'path': 'plugins/static-analysis/skills/semgrep/references/rulesets.md'}}, {'id': 'SAS-022', 'severity': 'Medium', 'category': 'Semgrep Language Ruleset', 'tool': 'Semgrep', 'name': 'Semgrep GA Language Rulesets', 'description': 'Add production-ready Semgrep language rulesets based on detected file extensions and frameworks.', 'match_strategy': 'language_ruleset', 'languages': [{'detection': '.py', 'primary_ruleset': 'p/python', 'framework_rulesets': ['p/django', 'p/flask', 'p/fastapi']}, {'detection': '.js,.jsx', 'primary_ruleset': 'p/javascript', 'framework_rulesets': ['p/react', 'p/nodejs', 'p/express', 'p/nextjs', 'p/angular']}, {'detection': '.ts,.tsx', 'primary_ruleset': 'p/typescript', 'framework_rulesets': ['p/react', 'p/nodejs', 'p/express', 'p/nextjs', 'p/angular']}, {'detection': '.go', 'primary_ruleset': 'p/golang', 'framework_rulesets': ['p/go']}, {'detection': '.java', 'primary_ruleset': 'p/java', 'framework_rulesets': ['p/spring', 'p/findsecbugs']}, {'detection': '.kt', 'primary_ruleset': 'p/kotlin', 'framework_rulesets': ['p/spring']}, {'detection': '.rb', 'primary_ruleset': 'p/ruby', 'framework_rulesets': ['p/rails']}, {'detection': '.php', 'primary_ruleset': 'p/php', 'framework_rulesets': ['p/symfony', 'p/laravel', 'p/phpcs-security-audit']}, {'detection': '.c,.cpp,.h', 'primary_ruleset': 'p/c'}, {'detection': '.rs', 'primary_ruleset': 'p/rust'}, {'detection': '.cs', 'primary_ruleset': 'p/csharp'}, {'detection': '.scala', 'primary_ruleset': 'p/scala'}, {'detection': '.swift', 'primary_ruleset': 'p/swift'}], 'remediation': 'Include each detected primary language ruleset and matching framework rulesets.', 'source': {'project': 'trailofbits/skills', 'path': 'plugins/static-analysis/skills/semgrep/references/rulesets.md'}}, {'id': 'SAS-023', 'severity': 'Low', 'category': 'Semgrep Language Ruleset', 'tool': 'Semgrep', 'name': 'Semgrep Beta And Experimental Language Rulesets', 'description': 'Add Semgrep beta or experimental language coverage when matching files are present, and note expected limitations.', 'match_strategy': 'language_ruleset', 'languages': [{'detection': '.ex,.exs', 'primary_ruleset': 'p/elixir', 'notes': 'Pro recommended for best coverage.'}, {'detection': '.cls,.trigger', 'primary_ruleset': 'p/apex', 'notes': 'Salesforce; Pro recommended.'}, {'detection': '.sol', 'primary_ruleset': 'third-party Decurity smart-contract rules'}, {'detection': 'Dockerfile', 'primary_ruleset': 'p/dockerfile'}, {'detection': '.yaml,.yml', 'primary_ruleset': 'p/yaml'}, {'detection': '.json', 'primary_ruleset': 'r/json.aws'}, {'detection': 'Bash scripts', 'primary_ruleset': 'community support'}, {'detection': 'Cairo,Circom', 'primary_ruleset': 'experimental smart-contract support'}], 'remediation': 'Add beta or experimental coverage with explicit notes about false positives and missing coverage.', 'source': {'project': 'trailofbits/skills', 'path': 'plugins/static-analysis/skills/semgrep/references/rulesets.md'}}, {'id': 'SAS-024', 'severity': 'Medium', 'category': 'Semgrep Framework Ruleset', 'tool': 'Semgrep', 'name': 'Semgrep Framework Detection', 'description': 'Detect common frameworks and add matching Semgrep framework rulesets.', 'match_strategy': 'framework_detection', 'frameworks': [{'framework': 'Django', 'signals': ['settings.py', 'urls.py', 'django in requirements'], 'ruleset': 'p/django'}, {'framework': 'Flask', 'signals': ['flask in requirements', '@app.route'], 'ruleset': 'p/flask'}, {'framework': 'FastAPI', 'signals': ['fastapi in requirements', '@app.get', '@app.post'], 'ruleset': 'p/fastapi'}, {'framework': 'React', 'signals': ['react dependency', '.jsx files', '.tsx files'], 'ruleset': 'p/react'}, {'framework': 'Next.js', 'signals': ['next.config.js', 'pages directory', 'app directory'], 'ruleset': 'p/nextjs'}, {'framework': 'Angular', 'signals': ['angular.json', '@angular dependencies'], 'ruleset': 'p/angular'}, {'framework': 'Express', 'signals': ['express dependency', 'app.use patterns'], 'ruleset': 'p/express'}, {'framework': 'NestJS', 'signals': ['@nestjs dependencies', '@Controller decorators'], 'ruleset': 'p/nodejs'}, {'framework': 'Spring', 'signals': ['pom.xml with spring', '@SpringBootApplication'], 'ruleset': 'p/spring'}, {'framework': 'Rails', 'signals': ['Gemfile with rails', 'config/routes.rb'], 'ruleset': 'p/rails'}, {'framework': 'Laravel', 'signals': ['composer.json with laravel', 'artisan'], 'ruleset': 'p/laravel'}, {'framework': 'Symfony', 'signals': ['composer.json with symfony', 'config/packages directory'], 'ruleset': 'p/symfony'}], 'remediation': 'Add framework-specific rulesets when framework signals are present.', 'source': {'project': 'trailofbits/skills', 'path': 'plugins/static-analysis/skills/semgrep/references/rulesets.md'}}, {'id': 'SAS-025', 'severity': 'Medium', 'category': 'Semgrep Infrastructure Ruleset', 'tool': 'Semgrep', 'name': 'Semgrep Infrastructure Rulesets', 'description': 'Add infrastructure and CI/CD Semgrep rulesets when matching files are present.', 'match_strategy': 'infrastructure_ruleset', 'rulesets': [{'detection': 'Dockerfile', 'ruleset': 'p/dockerfile', 'description': 'Container security and best practices.'}, {'detection': '.tf,.hcl', 'ruleset': 'p/terraform', 'description': 'IaC misconfigurations, CIS benchmarks, and cloud provider security.'}, {'detection': 'Kubernetes manifests', 'ruleset': 'p/kubernetes', 'description': 'Kubernetes security and RBAC issues.'}, {'detection': 'CloudFormation', 'ruleset': 'p/cloudformation', 'description': 'AWS infrastructure security.'}, {'detection': 'GitHub Actions', 'ruleset': 'p/github-actions', 'description': 'CI/CD security and secrets exposure.'}, {'detection': '.yaml,.yml', 'ruleset': 'p/yaml', 'description': 'Generic YAML patterns.'}, {'detection': 'AWS IAM JSON', 'ruleset': 'r/json.aws', 'description': 'IAM policy misconfiguration rules.'}], 'remediation': 'Include matching infrastructure rulesets for IaC, containers, CI/CD, and policy files.', 'source': {'project': 'trailofbits/skills', 'path': 'plugins/static-analysis/skills/semgrep/references/rulesets.md'}}, {'id': 'SAS-026', 'severity': 'High', 'category': 'Semgrep Third-Party Ruleset', 'tool': 'Semgrep', 'name': 'Required Third-Party Semgrep Rulesets', 'description': 'Include third-party Semgrep rule sources when language coverage matches; they are required because they catch vulnerabilities absent from official registry packs.', 'match_strategy': 'third_party_ruleset', 'third_party_sources': [{'languages': ['Python', 'Go', 'Ruby', 'JavaScript', 'TypeScript', 'Terraform', 'HCL'], 'source_name': 'Trail of Bits', 'source': 'https://github.com/trailofbits/semgrep-rules', 'reason': 'Security audit patterns from real engagements.'}, {'languages': ['C', 'C++'], 'source_name': 3562, 'source': 'https://github.com/0xdea/semgrep-rules', 'reason': 'Memory safety and low-level vulnerabilities.'}, {'languages': ['Solidity', 'Cairo', 'Rust'], 'source_name': 'Decurity', 'source': 'https://github.com/Decurity/semgrep-smart-contracts', 'reason': 'Smart contract and DeFi vulnerability patterns.'}, {'languages': ['Go'], 'source_name': 'dgryski', 'source': 'https://github.com/dgryski/semgrep-go', 'reason': 'Additional Go-specific patterns.'}, {'languages': ['Android Java', 'Kotlin'], 'source_name': 'MindedSecurity', 'source': 'https://github.com/mindedsecurity/semgrep-rules-android-security', 'reason': 'OWASP MASTG-derived mobile security rules.'}, {'languages': ['Java', 'Go', 'JavaScript', 'TypeScript', 'CSharp', 'Python', 'PHP'], 'source_name': 'elttam', 'source': 'https://github.com/elttam/semgrep-rules', 'reason': 'Security consulting patterns.'}, {'languages': ['Dockerfile', 'PHP', 'Go', 'Java'], 'source_name': 'kondukto', 'source': 'https://github.com/kondukto-io/semgrep-rules', 'reason': 'Container and web application security.'}, {'languages': ['PHP', 'Kotlin', 'Java'], 'source_name': 'dotta', 'source': 'https://github.com/federicodotta/semgrep-rules', 'reason': 'Pentest-derived web and mobile app rules.'}, {'languages': ['Terraform', 'HCL'], 'source_name': 'HashiCorp', 'source': 'https://github.com/hashicorp-forge/semgrep-rules', 'reason': 'HashiCorp infrastructure patterns.'}, {'languages': ['Swift', 'Java', 'Cobol'], 'source_name': 'akabe1', 'source': 'https://github.com/akabe1/akabe1-semgrep-rules', 'reason': 'iOS and legacy system patterns.'}, {'languages': ['Java'], 'source_name': 'Atlassian Labs', 'source': 'https://github.com/atlassian-labs/atlassian-sast-ruleset', 'reason': 'Atlassian-maintained Java rules.'}, {'languages': ['Python', 'JavaScript', 'TypeScript', 'Java', 'Ruby', 'Go', 'PHP'], 'source_name': 'Apiiro', 'source': 'https://github.com/apiiro/malicious-code-ruleset', 'reason': 'Malicious code and supply-chain detection.'}], 'remediation': 'Include matching third-party rule sources or explicitly document why they were excluded.', 'source': {'project': 'trailofbits/skills', 'path': 'plugins/static-analysis/skills/semgrep/references/rulesets.md'}}, {'id': 'SAS-027', 'severity': 'Medium', 'category': 'SARIF Processing', 'tool': 'SARIF', 'name': 'Validate SARIF Structure', 'description': 'Validate SARIF 2.1.0 structure before processing findings.', 'match_strategy': 'result_processing', 'requirements': ['Confirm version is 2.1.0.', 'Confirm runs array exists.', 'Confirm tool driver metadata exists.', 'Confirm results arrays are handled defensively.'], 'remediation': 'Reject or repair malformed SARIF before aggregation, filtering, or reporting.', 'source': {'project': 'trailofbits/skills', 'path': 'plugins/static-analysis/skills/sarif-parsing/SKILL.md'}}, {'id': 'SAS-028', 'severity': 'Medium', 'category': 'SARIF Processing', 'tool': 'SARIF', 'name': 'Normalize SARIF Paths', 'description': 'Normalize SARIF artifact URIs so findings can be compared across tools and environments.', 'match_strategy': 'result_processing', 'requirements': ['Remove file URI prefixes.', 'URL-decode paths.', 'Resolve relative paths against the target base path when needed.', 'Normalize path separators.'], 'remediation': 'Normalize paths before deduplication, baseline comparison, and reporting.', 'source': {'project': 'trailofbits/skills', 'path': 'plugins/static-analysis/skills/sarif-parsing/SKILL.md'}}, {'id': 'SAS-029', 'severity': 'Medium', 'category': 'SARIF Processing', 'tool': 'SARIF', 'name': 'Deduplicate SARIF Findings', 'description': 'Deduplicate SARIF results using stable fingerprints when available, with fallback keys based on rule, location, and snippet context.', 'match_strategy': 'result_processing', 'requirements': ['Prefer partialFingerprints or fingerprints.', 'Fall back to rule ID plus normalized location.', 'Preserve original runs and tool metadata when aggregating.'], 'remediation': 'Use stable fingerprints to identify duplicate findings across tools and repeated scans.', 'source': {'project': 'trailofbits/skills', 'path': 'plugins/static-analysis/skills/sarif-parsing/SKILL.md'}}, {'id': 'SAS-030', 'severity': 'Medium', 'category': 'Scan Quality', 'tool': 'Static Analysis', 'name': 'Investigate Zero Findings', 'description': 'Zero findings can indicate poor database quality, missing models, wrong rulesets, broken tool installation, or invalid SARIF rather than clean code.', 'match_strategy': 'quality_gate', 'applies_when': ['Any selected scanner returns zero findings.'], 'requirements': ['Verify target path and file counts.', 'Verify tool installation.', 'Verify rulesets loaded.', 'Verify CodeQL database quality when CodeQL was used.', 'Verify SARIF contains results when parsing existing output.'], 'remediation': 'Report zero findings only after validating scan coverage and tool quality.', 'source': {'project': 'trailofbits/skills', 'path': 'plugins/static-analysis/README.md'}}], 'default_match_strategy': 'unspecified', 'report_template': '# scan-static-analysis Report\n\n| Field | Value |\n|-------|-------|\n| Skill | scan-static-analysis |\n| Target | {{target}} |\n| Date | {{date}} |\n| Branch | {{branch}} |\n| Tools | {{tools}} |\n| Mode | {{mode}} |\n| Rulesets | {{rulesets}} |\n| Files Reviewed | {{file_count}} |\n| Total Findings | {{total_findings}} |\n| Overall Severity | {{overall_severity}} |\n\n---\n\n## Scan Plan\n\n**Target:** {{target}}\n\n**Output Directory:** {{output_directory}}\n\n**Tooling:** {{tools}}\n\n**Selected Rules:** {{selected_rules}}\n\n**Excluded Rules:** {{excluded_rules}}\n\n**Reasoning:** {{selection_reasoning}}\n\n## Findings\n\n{{#each findings}}\n### [{{severity}}] {{rule_id}} - {{rule_name}}\n\n**Tool:** {{tool}}\n**File:** `{{file}}` (line {{line}})\n**Category:** {{category}}\n**Message:** {{message}}\n**Confidence:** {{confidence}}\n**Impact:** {{impact}}\n\n```text\n{{snippet}}\n```\n\n**Remediation:** {{remediation}}\n\n---\n{{/each}}\n\n{{#if no_findings}}\nNo static-analysis findings were reported by the selected tools and rulesets.\n{{/if}}\n\n## Summary Table\n\n| Severity | Count |\n|----------|-------|\n| Critical | {{count_critical}} |\n| High     | {{count_high}} |\n| Medium   | {{count_medium}} |\n| Low      | {{count_low}} |\n| Info     | {{count_info}} |\n\n## Tool Quality Checks\n\n- CodeQL database quality: {{codeql_database_quality}}\n- Semgrep engine mode: {{semgrep_engine_mode}}\n- SARIF validation: {{sarif_validation}}\n- Zero-finding review: {{zero_finding_review}}\n\n## Next Steps\n\n- Address **Critical** and **High** findings before merging.\n- Review **Medium** findings and document accepted risk.\n- Re-run with `run-all` mode for manual audit coverage when time permits.\n- Preserve raw SARIF output for baselining, deduplication, and regression checks.\n'}
